Experiment 41: Automate Dropdown Selection Using selectByVisibleText() in Selenium WebDriver

# AIM
To automate dropdown selection using the `selectByVisibleText()` method in Selenium WebDriver and verify the selected option.

# ALGORITHM
1. Start the program.
2. Import the required Selenium WebDriver packages.
3. Create an instance of ChromeDriver.
4. Open the practice webpage.
5. Locate the dropdown element.
6. Create a Select class object.
7. Use `selectByVisibleText()` to select the required option.
8. Verify the selected option using `getFirstSelectedOption()`.
9. Validate the result using JUnit assertions.
10. Close the browser.
11. Stop the program.

# CODE

**File: DropdownSelectionTest.java**

```java
import org.openqa.selenium.By;
import org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.WebElement;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.support.ui.Select;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class DropdownSelectionTest {

    @Test
    public void testDropdownSelection() {

        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.get("https://the-internet.herokuapp.com/dropdown");

            WebElement dropdown =
                driver.findElement(By.id("dropdown"));

            Select select = new Select(dropdown);

            select.selectByVisibleText("Option 2");

            String selectedOption =
                select.getFirstSelectedOption().getText();

            System.out.println("Selected Option: " + selectedOption);

            assertEquals("Option 2", selectedOption);

            System.out.println("Dropdown selection successful.");

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}
```

